WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
New Relic is chosen for observability. Before it starts, Deploy warns if the cluster is short of room.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The deployment creates the newrelic namespace, stores the licence key as a Kubernetes secret, and adds the New Relic Helm repository.

3
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:56.000
It installs the New Relic bundle. The Containers view shows its pods start.

4
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Validation checks the Kubernetes API, the namespace, the licence secret, 3 deployments, 3 daemonsets, 6 of 6 pods ready, and that New Relic accepts the licence key. Every check passes.

5
00:01:32.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Next it creates the New Relic dashboards.

6
00:02:53.000 --> 00:03:05.000
There is an assessment dashboard and a workload dashboard for each database, plus platform overviews.

7
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Connection Info links straight to the dashboards.

8
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:58.000
The PostgreSQL workload dashboard opens in New Relic. It is empty for now, because the database is not registered yet.

9
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Back in the Kubernetes Monitor, the New Relic pods are running.

10
00:04:12.000 --> 00:05:05.000
The deployment finishes its last steps.

11
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:19.000
New Relic is deployed in 4 minutes 57 seconds.

